<title>PORTUGAL: First Austrian bank launches 5 bln esc Navigator.</title>
<headline>First Austrian bank launches 5 bln esc Navigator.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Austrian Bank launched a five billion escudo five-year Navigator indexed to six-month Lisbor, leader Banco Essi said.</p>
<p>ISSUER: First Austrian Bank</p>
<p>RATING: A1 (Moody's)</p>
<p>AMOUNT: 5 bln esc</p>
<p>MATURITY: 5 yrs</p>
<p>NOMINAL INTEREST RATE: 6-month Lisbor</p>
<p>ISSUE PRICE: 100 percent</p>
<p>NOMINAL VALUE: 1,000,000 escudos</p>
<p>ISSUE PRICE: 100 pct</p>
<p>LIQUIDATION DATE: 5 Aug 1997</p>
<p>PAYMENT OF INTEREST: Every six months</p>
<p>REIMBURSEMENT: At par, at end of 5-year term</p>
<p>ADMISSION TO QUOTATION: Luxembourg bourse</p>
<p>LAW APPLICABLE: English law</p>
<p>NATIONAL PAYING AGENT: Banco ESSI SA</p>
<p>LEADER: Banco ESSI SA</p>
<p>PRINCIPAL PAYING AGENT: Kredietbank Luxembourg</p>
</text>
